The task was to find the maximum area of an axis-aligned rectangle formed by four points from a given set such that no other point lies inside or on its border.

I've implemented this in `solution.py` by:
1. Iterating through all combinations of 4 points from the input list.
2. Checking if each combination forms an axis-aligned rectangle (exactly two unique x-coordinates and two unique y-coordinates, with four distinct points).
3. Verifying that no other point from the input set lies within or on the boundary of this rectangle.
4. Keeping track of the maximum area found among all valid rectangles.

The solution has been verified against the provided test cases using `sh run_tests.sh`.
